syntax:
extern "C" {
    // Declaration of C-compatible functions or variables
    void someCFunction(int arg);  // No name mangling; symbol is 'someCFunction'
}

Implementation notes: The extern "C" block instructs the compiler to use C linkage for the enclosed declarations. For functions, this means the compiler will not apply C++ name mangling. If mixing with C++ features, ensure that the function signatures match exactly between C and C++ to avoid ABI mismatches, such as differences in struct padding or calling conventions as per the referenced standards.
